# Sample StorageClass for GKE Substrate integration with GCP Filestore VolumePools.
#
# VolumePools (FiFA Fast Availability) provide sub-second dynamic volume claims from
# pre-warmed Filestore multi-share instances.
#
# Usage (Automated):
#   Use the deployment script to dynamically render and apply this template:
#   deploy.sh --project-id <PROJECT_ID> --volumepool-location <LOCATION> --volumepool-name <VOLUMEPOOL_NAME>
#
# Usage (Manual):
#   1. Copy this template to a new file (e.g., storageclass.yaml).
#   2. Replace <PROJECT_ID>, <LOCATION>, <VOLUMEPOOL_NAME>, and <STORAGECLASS_NAME>.
#   3. Apply: kubectl apply -f storageclass.yaml
#
# Mount options note:
#   Agent Substrate reads only StorageClass.provisioner and StorageClass.parameters
#   and ignores StorageClass.mountOptions, so NFS client options must be set under
#   parameters.mount-options.
#   - The value is ONE comma-separated string with no spaces. Never fold it with a
#     YAML ">" or "|" block scalar, which would add spaces or newlines.
#   - Any value replaces all of the CSI driver's default mount options, so list
#     every option you want.
#   - nconnect=8 requires Linux kernel 5.3 or later; older kernels fail to mount
#     and need explicit parameters.mount-options without nconnect. Linux shares
#     one NFS client per server IP, so nconnect takes effect for a server IP only
#     once every earlier mount to that IP on the node is unmounted.
#   - port=2049 and mountport=2050 are fixed (skipping rpcbind).
#   - Privileged source-port budget: Linux NFS binds TCP connections to ports
#     665-1023 by default (about 360 per node). With nconnect=8, each distinct
#     server IP a node mounts uses 8 ports, so a node caps out at roughly 44
#     distinct server IPs (fewer with other NFS mounts and TIME_WAIT sockets).
#     If a node hits that limit, set parameters.mount-options with a lower
#     nconnect.
#   - nolock and actimeo=60 are only safe for dedicated single-actor workspaces
#     where strictly one node mounts a volume at a time and the runtime unmounts
#     it on the old node before mounting on the new one. Do NOT use this
#     StorageClass for regular Kubernetes PVCs (neither ReadWriteOnce nor
#     ReadWriteMany -- the CSIDriver sets attachRequired: false, so even
#     ReadWriteOnce PVCs can overlap across two nodes during rolling updates) or
#     for volumes shared by several actors. Otherwise, nolock gives no
#     cross-node lock exclusion (corruption risk) and actimeo=60 can serve up to
#     60 seconds of stale file/directory attributes and negative lookups. Create a
#     separate StorageClass without nolock and actimeo=60 for those workloads.
#   - StorageClass parameters can't be changed after creation. To change them,
#     replace or delete and re-create the StorageClass. Existing volumes keep the
#     mount-options value they were created with.

apiVersion: storage.k8s.io/v1
kind: StorageClass
metadata:
  name: <STORAGECLASS_NAME>
provisioner: filestore.csi.storage.gke.io
parameters:
  volume-pool: "projects/<PROJECT_ID>/locations/<LOCATION>/volumePools/<VOLUMEPOOL_NAME>"
  mount-options: "vers=3,proto=tcp,mountproto=tcp,port=2049,mountport=2050,nolock,nconnect=8,rsize=524288,wsize=524288,actimeo=60"
allowVolumeExpansion: false
reclaimPolicy: Delete
volumeBindingMode: Immediate
